      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T12:25:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve created the following issues[1][2] to track 2 problems that where introduced when this useful feature was introduced. \nI believe [1] is not controversial and should be easy enough to fix.\n[2] has a broader scope and will require some agreement amongst members of the community.\n\n[1] https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/405035566\n[2] https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/405004972",
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c19c1ea2_a96b8a97",
        "filename": "Documentation/rest-api-accounts.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 196,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T11:34:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should explain here was _deletes_ actually means, also that it is not a *complete* deletion, because the account identity will remain forever in the changes and respositories that the user has contributed to.\n\nDeleting that account information permanently won\u0027t be possible, unless you perform a complete history rewrite.",
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5533470a_ceee2a4b",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/StarredChangesUtil.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 300,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T11:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this `skipInvalidChanges` needed? How is this related to the removal of an account?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 300,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 300,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2906a36_3a755286",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/AccountsUpdate.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 562,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T11:34:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of completely removing the refs, why not just updating it and pointing to a a _tumbstone_ BLOB? So that it can still be resolved but point to nothing and we have a memory that the account existed but was removed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 562,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 562,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "861f4d09_b59b1bed",
        "filename": "javatests/com/google/gerrit/acceptance/api/accounts/AccountIT.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 3232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T11:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see a few tests missing:\n\n1. You should create a group with the account to be deleted inside it\n2. After the account deletion, the group would still be consistent\n3. It is possible to remove the deleted account from the group\n4. The account deleted should still return _something_ (a tombstone maybe?) when the changes he created are fetched \n5. The account deleted should still return _something_ (a tombstone maybe?) when the messages posted on changes are fetched",
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc1f6e80_c1a51bef",
        "filename": "javatests/com/google/gerrit/acceptance/api/accounts/AccountIT.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 3244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T11:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe Gerrit will continue to reference the account-id: why not returning a tumbstone instead? Returning an exception will then break the Gerrit UX.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3243,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 3244,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ec67b41_735ad9f7",
        "filename": "javatests/com/google/gerrit/acceptance/api/accounts/AccountIT.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 3248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1155599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T12:25:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has the potential to leave Gerrit in an inconsistent state. Account IDs are referenced in many parts of Gerrit, including group membership and all the reviews that that user did to changes or reviews.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3248,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 3248,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68cafaf4_bb795ec3",
        "filename": "javatests/com/google/gerrit/acceptance/api/accounts/AccountIT.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 3248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T09:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed, this has created the Issue 405035566.\n\nI believe the id should stay, but as anonymous and disabled, similar of what my `accounts` plugin was doing at https://gerrit.googlesource.com/plugins/account/+/refs/heads/master/src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/plugins/account/GerritAccountRemover.java#90.\n\n```suggestion\n    assertThat(gApi.accounts().query(deleted.id().toString()).get()).isNotEmpty();\n```\n\n@nitzan@google.com WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "1ec67b41_735ad9f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3248,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 3248,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "4afacfab28e4e895fb8da9f0410f70e62ec5f851",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
